    {
      "id": "claim_10e84ad88e5e48fb838ba34ee8c1295f",
      "statement": "The repository is a monorepo of independently versioned packages under libs/, each with its own pyproject.toml, Makefile, and README.md, with no root pyproject.toml, so work happens inside the package being changed.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://libs/DEVELOPMENT.md#L30-L49",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:7fadcab0884d15474b9ffc94632e833e341967e49cdc798b113d09d8d854a6f2:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_044aca744c614b14a955c84343818c66",
      "statement": "Deep Agents is layered: the deepagents harness sits on top of LangChain's create_agent, which sits on top of the LangGraph runtime; identifying which layer owns a behavior narrows where to look.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://libs/ARCHITECTURE.md#L12-L30",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:591b743f68a1f0d4a3711e21813aa4b1e01123fccc91f89bd8eb5d94bab5187e:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_8d05af551d914ba9b6567fee0f93d9d3",
      "statement": "The recommended navigation heuristic is to trace from a create_deep_agent() argument to the middleware or backend it installs, then follow how that component participates during execution; missing tools point to middleware assembly and profile exclusions, while visible-but-failing tools point to backend capability and permission enforcement.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://libs/ARCHITECTURE.md#L104-L115",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:5f90d7982713ac6aef83786a9912bf4e685bdb8cb673bd3231cdaab096fabc7b:"
